  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 321 AM EDT Sun Aug 16 2026\n\n- Scattered showers and storms today\n\nScattered showers and thunderstorms are expected in the vicinity\nof an MCV moving from northern Illinois to southern Michigan this\nmorning, then ahead of a weak cold front sweeping through the \nstate this afternoon. CAPE values 500-1000 J/kg are confined\nmainly south of I-96 this morning, though may extend farther \nnorth for a time around mid day. Storm cells should be fairly \nlimited in organization given about 20 knots of 0-6 km shear. PW \naround 2 inches will make for efficient rainfall rates, though \nlimited updraft width and scattered coverage of cells would favor \njust isolated spots of 1-2 inch totals, highest probability south \nof I-96 per the HREF.\n\n- Shower/storm chances late Tue to early Wed, and late week\n\nMonday will bring relief from the humidity, as dew points drop to\naround or below 60. Some moisture and slightly warmer air from the\ncentral CONUS returns on Tuesday, ahead of a cold front that will\nsag through on Wednesday, nudged south as an upper-level low \nlumbers across Hudson Bay and northern Ontario. Scattered\nthunderstorms are again possible in the vicinity of this front\nmainly between Tue evening and early Wed morning, as a majority \nof ENS and GEFS members indicate. Instability is still a little in\nquestion, as most solutions project fairly modest amounts in the \nballpark of 500-1000 J/kg, though a few offer closer to 2000 J/kg.\nThis would be something to monitor for a marginal severe threat, \nas deep-layer shear will be greater than it is today.\n\nA majority of ensemble member solutions favor drier and somewhat\ncooler air for later Wed into Thursday, followed by another modest\nmoisture return late Friday into Saturday with a chance for more\nscattered showers or storms. Naturally, this is lower confidence \nthis far out, given the increasing spread in the solution \nenvelope.",
